# This branch carries the FROZEN RELEASE, not only the source package. On top
# of src/, configs/, notebooks/, scripts/, tests/, README and the environment
# lock, results/, figures/, resolved_configs/, manifests/ and
# executed_notebooks/ are tracked here so the evidence behind every figure
# lives at the same revision as the code that produced it.
#
# The E4 reference sample banks are written as uncompressed float64 .npz and
# exceed GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, so they go through git-lfs; see
# .gitattributes. `scripts/build_release.py --frozen` still zips the working
# tree for a standalone archive.

dist/

# Reusable numerical caches. These stay untracked: they are keyed by device and
# software version, so another machine must measure its own rather than adopt
# ours. Every one of them rebuilds on demand.
cache/
.matplotlib-cache/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

*.log
.DS_Store

# Internal working notes, kept local.
REVISION_NOTES.md
REVISION_NOTES_manuscript.md

# E4's reference build never passed its frozen acceptance gates, so
# reference_validated is false and no run may cite it. Its raw PT and SNIS
# sample banks are 110 MB and 519 MB of uncompressed float64 -- both over
# GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, and not worth ~630 MB of LFS quota for data
# nothing is allowed to use. The substantive evidence, reference_validation.json
# with its 73 gate records, is tracked. Regenerate the banks with
# `python scripts/build_reference.py E4`.
results/E4_coupled_quartic_chain/reference/reference_samples_24d.npz
results/E4_coupled_quartic_chain/reference/reference_snis_weighted_24d.npz
